# Golden traces are byte-exact fixtures: the trace format requires LF-only
# line endings with a trailing newline, and CI validates that byte-for-byte
# on every OS. Force LF in the working tree so a CRLF-defaulted checkout
# (Git for Windows) cannot corrupt what the validator checks.
*.ndjson text eol=lf

# The schema/ artifacts are generated in canonical form (sorted keys, LF,
# trailing newline) and CI's freshness gate byte-compares a regeneration
# against the committed file. Force LF so a CRLF-defaulted checkout cannot
# make a fresh artifact look stale on Windows.
*.schema.json text eol=lf

